    "text": "To solve the equation \\(3^{2x^2 - 5x + 2} = 3^{2x^2 + 7x - 4}\\), we can use the property of exponents that states if \\(a^m = a^n\\), then \\(m = n\\). Therefore, we can set the exponents equal to each other:\n\n\\[2x^2 - 5x + 2 = 2x^2 + 7x - 4\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the equation by subtracting \\(2x^2\\) from both sides:\n\n\\[-5x + 2 = 7x - 4\\]\n\nThen, we add \\(5x\\) to both sides to get all the \\(x\\) terms on one side:\n\n\\[2 = 12x - 4\\]\n\nNext, we add 4 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[6 = 12x\\]\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by 12 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x = \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2}\\]\n\nSo the value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\).",
